[00:00.00] 作词 : Emily Sparks
[00:00.67] 作曲 : Emily Sparks
[00:01.34]I saw her mother this morning
[00:07.38]At the downtown cafe
[00:10.57]Staring blankly Down in morning
[00:16.02]Had her cup of gourmet coffee
[00:19.29]And she asked me "What her baby’d been missing"
[00:24.84]And I shake my head
[00:28.03]Can’t think of nothing
[00:30.14]But candy wrappers
[00:33.09]tucked into the folds of the bed
[00:37.26]And how I don’t see them around
[00:42.00]Since Sarah left town
[00:46.68]
[01:02.15]Now people always think they know you
[01:07.53]And they’re almost always wrong
[01:11.07]Tried to bend you till they broke you
[01:16.69]So she moved along
[01:20.71]And sometimes I see them around
[01:25.38]Since Sarah left town
[01:29.42]Trying to track her down
[01:36.84]Sarah，Sarah
[01:45.90]Sarah，Sarah
[02:03.42]She’s chasing her soul
[02:07.81]Not running away
[02:12.19]If you'd just let her go
[02:17.03]She’ll know the way
[02:21.23]And I saw her mother this morning
[02:26.33]She looked me in the eye
[02:29.69]they can not know, sometimes I think I hear her laughing
[02:35.14]And all I can do is cry
[02:38.99]And it's a funny thing about people
[02:43.86]How everyone has a song
[02:47.58]And he sings it every moment
[02:51.90]But we don't hear it until he's gone
[02:57.06]And sometimes I see them around
[03:01.74]Since Sarah left town
[03:05.45]They’re humming with heads hanging down
[03:13.62]en...
[03:22.04]en...
[03:30.52]Sarah，Sarah
[03:39.03]Sarah，Sarah
